{
  "note": "The module surface and the live shape of the objects that cross it. Shapes are observed, not declared: \"function/3\" means arity 3, \"array[8] of object\" is a real length from a real race. Regenerate with `node tools/port-export.js`.",
  "entryPoints": {
    "createRace(opts)": "builds a race. opts: seed, stageIndex, playerType, gc, leaders, div, and optionally kit, route, playerStats, out, gears, payMul. Consumes the seeded PRNG to draw the course — this is the call whose determinism matters most.",
    "step(race, dt, input)": "advance ONE fixed tick. dt is always CFG.fixedDt. `input` is the player's controls, or null to let the sim's own AI ride the player (which is what ladder.js and dominance.js do, and why they cannot see player-input mechanics).",
    "settle(race)": "final classification: the finishing order with places, times and points.",
    "snapshot(race) / restore(snap, opts)": "serialise a race between stages of a tour. Only SAVE_KEYS survive; anything else re-derives within a few frames, deliberately.",
    "secondChance(race)": "the post-crash revival and convoy chase.",
    "gradeAt / elevAt / altAt / windAt / centreAt / widthAt / edgeAt / bendAt / curveAt": "course lookups by distance. Pure functions of the course; the view uses them too."
  },
